The code statements that fix the bug are:
mutex_unlock(&tp->control);
if (!runtime_resume && test_bit(RTL8152_INACCESSIBLE, &tp->flags))
	usb_reset_device(tp->udev);
Reason:
The `usb_reset_device()` call is moved to after releasing the `tp->control` mutex. This prevents the recursive lock attempt because the reset now occurs outside the mutex‑protected region. The condition also ensures the reset only happens for system resume (not runtime resume), preserving the original intent while avoiding the deadlock.

